Record must simply add the record to the existing RRset.'}]}, {'group': 'Add Existing RRset – SOA replacement', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'r', 'value': 'SOARecord with name = zone.getOrigin() (e.g., example.com.) and new serial number'}], 'expected': "The previous SOA record is removed from the RRset, the zone's internal soaRecord field is updated to the new SOARecord, and the RRset now contains only the new SOA record.", 'description': "When an existing RRset is found and the incoming record is a SOA, addRecord must delete the old SOA from the RRset, replace the zone's soaRecord reference, and add the new SOA."}]}, {'group': 'First SOA Addition', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'r', 'value': 'SOARecord with name = zone.getOrigin() (e.g., new Name("example.com.")), serial = 2023100101, mname = new Name("ns.example.com."), rname = new Name("hostmaster.example.com."), refresh = 3600, retry = 600, expire = 604800, minimum = 86400'}], 'expected': 'No exception thrown. Zone.soaRecord is set to the added SOARecord. A new RRset for name example.com. with type SOA exists containing exactly one record (the added SOA).', 'description': 'When the zone has no existing SOA, adding a valid SOA record should store it, update the internal soaRecord field, and create an RRset containing only that SOA.'}]}, {'group': 'Apex NS Record', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'r', 'value': 'NSRecord with name = zone.getOrigin() (e.g., new Name("example.com.")), target = new Name("ns1.example.com.")'}], 'expected': 'No exception thrown. A new RRset for name example.com. with type NS is created and contains the added NSRecord. Zone.soaRecord (if previously set) remains unchanged.', 'description': 'Adding a non‑SOA record whose name equals the zone origin should be allowed; the record is stored in its own RRset and does not affect the SOA handling.'}]}, {'group': 'Duplicate Record Ignored', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'r', 'value': 'A Record with name = new Name("dup.example.com."), address = 192.0.2.1'}], 'expected': 'First call: RRset for dup.example.com./A created with one record. Second call (same record): No exception; RRset still contains exactly one record (duplicate is ignored).', 'description': 'Adding the same Record object twice should not create duplicate entries inside the RRset; the RRset size remains unchanged after the second addition.'}]}, {'group': 'Deep Subdomain Record', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'r', 'value': 'A Record with name = new Name("host.deep.sub.example.com."), address = 198.51.100.42'}], 'expected': 'No exception thrown. A new RRset for name host.deep.sub.example.com. with type A is created containing the record. The subdomain check passes because the name is a subdomain of the zone origin (example.com.).', 'description': 'Verifies that the method correctly recognises multi‑level subdomains as valid members of the zone.'}]}, {'group': 'RRset Size Increment', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'r', 'value': 'A Record with name = new Name("multi.example.com."), address = 203.0.113.5'}], 'expected': 'First call creates RRset with one record. Second call with a different A record (address = 203.0.113.6) adds to the same RRset, resulting in exactly two records in the RRset. No exception thrown.', 'description': 'When an RRset already exists for a name/type, adding another record of the same type should increase the RRset size accordingly.'}]}]
